{% liquid
  comment
    Renders images within the mobile menu if mobile menu image blocks are added in the header.

    Required parameters:
      - link: { Object } The link within a menu that has enabled the mobile menu images block.
      - aspect_ratio: { String } The block setting's aspect ratio to apply to the image. Can be:
        - Natural, Square, Portrait, Landscape
      - thumbnail_width: { Number } The block setting's thumbnail width to apply to the image.

    Optional parameters:
      - size: { String } 'large' renders one big category image (used for the
        drill-down second-level panel) instead of the small inline row
        thumbnail. Omit for the original small-thumbnail behavior.
      - custom_image: { Object } An explicit image (from the block's own
        "custom_image" image_picker setting) that takes priority over the
        metafield/collection/product fallback chain below.
  endcomment

  assign resource = link.object

  if custom_image != blank
    assign thumbnail_image = custom_image
  elsif resource.metafields.stiletto.mobile_menu_thumbnail != blank
    assign thumbnail_image = resource.metafields.stiletto.mobile_menu_thumbnail.value
  endif

  unless thumbnail_image
    case link.type
      when 'collection_link'
        assign thumbnail_image = resource.image | default: resource.products.first.featured_image
      when 'product_link'
        assign thumbnail_image = resource.featured_image
    endcase
  endunless
%}

{% if thumbnail_image %}
  {% if size == 'large' %}
    <div class="drawer-menu__category-image">
      {%- comment -%}
        On desktop this covers a full-height column (~2x taller than
        wide) — object-fit:cover scales by height there, not by the
        column's own width, so a sizes hint proportional to width alone
        under-requests resolution badly. src_set_type 'thumbnail' also
        caps out at 600px, nowhere near enough for a near-full-viewport-
        height crop. 'grid' (up to 2200px) + an inflated sizes value
        (accounting for the height-driven scale-up) keeps it sharp.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {% render 'image', image: thumbnail_image, aspect_ratio: aspect_ratio, sizes: '(min-width: 960px) 60vw, 100vw', src_set_type: 'grid' %}
    </div>
  {% else %}
    <div
      class="drawer-menu__link-thumbnail"
      style="--thumbnail-width:{{ thumbnail_width }}px"
    >
      {% render 'image', image: thumbnail_image, aspect_ratio: aspect_ratio, sizes: '200px', src_set_type: 'thumbnail' %}
    </div>
  {% endif %}
{% endif %}
